A1. The cause of a good many blowouts. (Two words) ~ NEWYEARS
A9. High spirits. ~ LIQUOR
A14. A bloomer that's a favorite in the South. ~ OLEANDER
A15. The aftermath of New Year's Eve. (abbr.) ~ AM
A16. A teetotaler with a very good record. ~ PRO
A17. A peach of a state to be in. (abbr.) ~ GA
A18. What the cook opened before dinner. ~ POD
A19. These appreciate a good port. ~ SHIPS
A22. How each got sentenced to a shorter term. ~ EA
A23. There's nothing supernatural about this spirit raiser. ~ GIN
A25. An old soak. ~ WET
A27. Food receptacles for the barnyard. ~ CROPS
A29. Feeding stalls. ~ INNS
A31. When this is broken it gets plastered. ~ RIB
A33. Reel people. ~ DRUNKS
A35. The way to be wed to be happy. ~ NEWLY
A37. Give this a ring sometime, girls. ~ EAR
A39. This is good, bad, or indifferent according to your nature. ~ TRAIT
A40. One thing a Quaker is profligate with. ~ YEA
A42. A powder that will do away with all your complexion troubles. ~ GUN
A44. This belongs to the pitcher's league. ~ TINE
A45. What you catch in bad weather besides a cold. ~ CAB
A48. A carriage that may land you in the ditch. ~ STAGGER
A51. Lousy Greek Restaurant (abbr.) ~ LGR
A52. The lowdown. ~ ALOW
A54. A time piece. ~ ERA
A55. Keep this on your husband New Year's Eve. ~ TAB
A57. A turn over that will shape things just the way you want them. ~ LATHE
A59. When this gets boiled it's hard to handle. ~ EGG
A61. This should be talked over at dinner. ~ TABLE
A65. What a girl uses to fetch and carry. ~ ESCORT
A67. A goddess the milkman should worship. ~ EOS
A69. Dance of the spirits. ~ REEL
A70. There's no place like them. ~ HOMES
A72. Bottled water. ~ DAM
A74. The kind of I trouble an operation won't help. ~ EGO
A75. Baby talk. ~ DA
A77. A good guide to go by. ~ PILOT
