A81. A coast to coast network. (abbr.) ~ AP
A82. A lot of people get a kick out of this. ~ ALE
A84. This makes not long, short. ~ NL
A85. The kind of desire that's seldom fulfilled. ~ ULTIMATE
A88. These are likely to cook your goose. ~ RANGES
A89. This will drive a pair to drink. ~ TEAMSTER

D1. A mug that can't hold much liquor. ~ NOGGIN
D2. The maid that almost upset the Round Table. ~ ELAINE
D3. A get-together. ~ WE
D4. Fido's SOS. ~ YAP
D5. This is enough for any poet. ~ ENOW
D6. What Cleopatra used for an exit. ~ ADDER
D7. A note that's easy to meet. ~ RE
D8. These take a hiding every June. (abbr.) ~ SRS
D9. What a man becomes when he's lorded in Scotland. ~ LAIRD
